    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Each division by 4 gives the next digit, starting with the units digit. The quotient contains the remaining higher place values, so reading the remainders backwards gives $213_4$.",
      "worked": "Dividing by 4 separates the units remainder from groups of 4. Dividing the quotient again separates groups of 4 from groups of $4^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}39&=4\\times9+3\\\\9&=4\\times2+1\\\\2&=4\\times0+2.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting the quotients back gives\n$$\\begin{align*}39&=4(4\\times2+1)+3\\\\39&=2\\times4^2+1\\times4+3\\\\39_{10}&=213_4.\\end{align*}$$\nThe remainders are found from the lowest place value upwards, so reversing their order puts the digits in the usual highest-to-lowest place-value order.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
